1. Removed the dependency on Sheet components
2. Created a simplified `PreviewSheetHeader` component that mimics the layout and functionality of the real SheetHeader
3. Implemented a basic close button without Dialog dependencies
4. Added a container with padding and border to better visualize the component
5. Maintained all the existing props and state management
6. Kept the same visual structure but removed the complex Dialog context requirements

This approach should work because:
1. It maintains the same visual appearance and functionality for preview purposes
2. It removes the dependency on Dialog context which was causing the error
3. It still allows testing of the `showCloseButton` and `className` props
4. It provides a good representation of how the component will look in actual usage

The preview should now render without the Dialog context error while still providing a meaningful representation of the SheetHeader component.

